   "l": "To the end of the body, no toil.",
   "v": true,
   "i": "and all your life you are never worn out.",
   "n": "終身 is built exactly like 沒身 two units back and means the same thing: for the whole of a life. Wang Bi's gloss is 無事永逸 — 'nothing to attend to, and ease for ever'.\n\nThat this unit is four characters long is not our doing. The sense-units of this text are the places where Wang Bi's commentary breaks into it, and he stopped here."
